{
  "rule": {
    "profile": "g2-recompute-vs-spill-v1",
    "G1": "for k in 1,2,4 and both stores (pinned RAM, direct NVMe spill): per-micro-batch losses (forward) and nonzero LoRA grads (backward) torch.equal to GA AND to the recompute L2L step; references reproducible (GA vs GA), else the --deterministic rerun; the controls must hold: identity saved-tensor hooks without a reload must raise or give different grads, a corrupted record must change the grads and leave the losses equal; and the records hold activation bytes only (0 weight bytes)",
    "G2": "bytes: every record holds exactly its activation items (payload == sum of the activation storages saved) and no streamed weight; the spilled bytes written and read per step equal spill_layers x k x record_capacity",
    "G3": "ram_store_vs_recompute (weights in RAM, records in pinned RAM): per-block step-time ratio B (store) / A (recompute), two-sided 95% t interval: pass if its upper bound < 0.95, fail if its lower bound >= 0.95, else no verdict",
    "G4": "disk_spill_vs_recompute (weights streamed from disk, records spilled to the weights' drive): the same ratio and bounds as G3",
    "V1": "device cuda; a CPU or synthetic session never gets a verdict",
    "V2": "required F1 checks (suspend, power, foreign_reads) ok on every arm a gate reads; a block with a void arm is replaced, an unknown one removes the gate",
    "V3": "every spilling store and the sustained I/O arms are direct (unbuffered)",
    "V4": "A and B of a block train on the same token rows (ids fingerprint)",
    "V5": "finite losses on every timed step",
    "V6": "every B arm wrote and read exactly its planned record bytes; A arms wrote none",
    "V7": "the F1 repeats rule has no block left to add (blocks_to_add == 0)",
    "V8": "disk-tier arms: the weight source reads with direct I/O",
    "V10": "disk-tier arms: the OS placement records (resolved path, mount, whole physical disk) show the records' spill directory and the weight shards on one physical disk; unknown placement removes the gate (direct-I/O flags are no evidence)",
    "V9": "the break-even inputs are sustained: g2_disk arms with status candidate, a fixture larger than RAM and >= 1800 s each; else the break-even is reported as an estimate only",
    "V11": "the sustained rates are bound to the disk-tier profile: every valid g2_disk arm and the profile name one machine id, and the arms' spill / weight disks are the profile's; a mismatch or an unknown identity makes the break-even an estimate",
    "V12": "label only, no gate status depends on it: a disk-tier gate and the break-even name the disk kind from the placement records (virtio vendor 0x1af4, a hypervisor's model string, a vd*/xvd* device); on a VIRTUAL disk they describe that virtual disk at that time, not a physical NVMe",
    "breakeven": "informational: saved recompute seconds per step against write + read + weight-read contention + store overhead, serial and overlapped; the store overhead is packing and host copies with the measured spill I/O waits taken out, so the drive is charged once, from its sustained rates; the 1.5x ceiling is a FLOP ratio, never a measured speed-up",
    "order": "A-B-B-A blocks, fresh process per arm"
  },
